  "answer": "I'll look through how product special prices are saved and how the storefront decides whether a discount is active.The discount is dropped in two places: product create writes the special end date into the start-date field, and price calculation then checks the start date a second time instead of the end date. I'll correct both.A product created through the admin API stored its special end date in the start-date field (`PersistableProductAvailabilityMapper`), and the storefront price calculation then compared that start date with itself instead of checking that the end date was still in the future (`ProductPriceUtils.finalPrice`). Both now keep and honor the end date, so a special with an end date (with or without a start date) is applied while it is active. Undated specials are unchanged.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-core,sm-shop -am compile -DskipTests\"], \"result\": \"not-run\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"storefront discount for a special price that has an end date, with and without a start date\"], \"missing\": [\"a unit test around ProductPriceUtils final-price discount windows\"]}",
